{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalNodeForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalNodeForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalParam","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.LagrangeCoeffSum","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SchurPrincipalBetaForm","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.zpow_node_dictionary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.zpow_node_dictionary","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalNodeForm.lean#L102-L108","doc":"The dictionary in the form `seminormalParam_node_form` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.axialDistance_corner_addable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.axialDistance_corner_addable","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalNodeForm.lean#L83-L100","doc":"**The content-to-β dictionary.**\n\nFor an addable cell in row `a` and a removable corner in row `b` of the same diagram, both rows\nbelow `r`,\n\n`axialDistance corner cell = β_a − β_b + 1`.\n\nAn addable cell has content `β_a − (r−1)`; a removable corner has content `β_b − r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.rowLen_of_isCornerCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.rowLen_of_isCornerCell","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalNodeForm.lean#L75-L81","doc":"A removable corner sits at the end of its row: `c = (b, μ_b − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.seminormalParam_one'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.seminormalParam_one'","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalNodeForm.lean#L62-L66","doc":"The `d = 1` value in the shape the `a = b` term of the corner identity produces:\n`(q − q⁻¹)·Q/(Q − 1) = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.seminormalParam_node_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.seminormalParam_node_form","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalNodeForm.lean#L39-L60","doc":"**The seminormal entry, in node coordinates.**\n\nWith `x_a`, `x_b` the nodes and `d` the axial distance, `Q^d·x_b = Q·x_a` turns\n\n`a(d) = (q − q⁻¹)/(1 − q^{−2d})`  into  `(q − q⁻¹)·Q·x_a/(Q·x_a − x_b)`,\n\nwhich is exactly the weight in `QOU.Mathlib.sum_prod_qratio_weighted`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}